meta {
  name: Assistant Slack OAuth Callback
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/hooks/assistant/slack/oauth?code={{slackOAuthCode}}&state={{slackOAuthState}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  code: {{slackOAuthCode}}
  state: {{slackOAuthState}}
}

docs {
  Where Slack redirects the admin's browser after "Add to Slack" (the
  app's OAuth redirect URL). Not called by clients — start from
  `Assistant/Channels - Slack Install`.

  **Auth.** No session; `state` is the encrypted value from the install
  URL (workspace, user, 15-minute expiry). Invalid state answers `400
  Invalid install link.`, expired `400`. `code` is exchanged with Slack
  (`oauth.v2.access`) for the bot token, saved per Slack team.

  Response is a `302` to `{frontend_url}/{workspace}/assistant?slack=`
  `connected` | `cancelled` (error or no code) | `failed` (Slack refused
  the code). Not reproducible by hand without a real Slack `code`.
}
